alifornia, Stan Ridgway, Chris Isaak y Smog. En Gran Bretaña, Billy Bragg, Robyn Hitchcock, Julian Cope y, la voz más importante de la década, Nick Cave, predicador del apocalipsis moral (From Her To Eternity, The Good Son). Sinéad O'Connor, Sting, Morrissey, Momus; el pop celta de Enya y Loreena McKennitt; al cambiar la década, Joe Henry, Daniel Lanois y Bob Mould.","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk y cantautores","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-80s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":104144116070442,"artist":"Chris Isaak","artist_id":270954935537263,"title":"Silvertone","year":1985,"ess":0,"yt":"haiHRd06i1Y","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores de los ochenta","scene_id":13391632264459,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.16"],"pages":[[1,186,null]]},{"id":1047818112874,"artist":"Chris Isaak","artist_id":270954935537263,"title":"Chris Isaak","year":1987,"ess":0,"yt":"BGMXxGIxzV4","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores de los ochenta","scene_id":13391632264459,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.16"],"pages":[[1,186,null]]},{"id":137898908612537,"artist":"Chris Isaak","artist_id":270954935537263,"title":"Wicked Game","year":1989,"ess":0,"yt":"jd-qI62gNJM","kind":"s","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores de los ochenta","scene_id":13391632264459,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.16"],"pages":[[1,186,null]]},{"id":67241011007974,"artist":"Chris Isaak","artist_id":270954935537263,"title":"Heart Shaped World","year":1989,"ess":0,"yt":"C45axx7xaIM","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores de los ochenta","scene_id":13391632264459,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.16"],"pages":[[1,186,null]]},{"id":237190183089593,"artist":"Chris Isaak","artist_id":270954935537263,"title":"San Francisco Days","year":1993,"ess":0,"yt":"Mqr-TzWqes0","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores de los ochenta","scene_id":13391632264459,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.16"],"pages":[[1,186,null]]},{"id":107098709615696,"artist":"Chris Isaak","artist_id":270954935537263,"title":"Forever Blue","year":1995,"ess":0,"yt":"_lRKtDuH33s","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores de los ochenta","scene_id":13391632264459,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.16"],"pages":[[1,186,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":186,"text":"…(ex-Blasters) specialized in moral and realistic vignettes, starting with Romeo's Escape (1988). San Francisco was graced by the isolated voice of Chris Isaak (2), a leftover from the \"Sixties revival\" movement who internalized Roy Orbison's romantic crooning, Elvis Presley's sobbing tenor, languid lounge…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":186,"text":"…not frightened, but rather impotent in the face of an immanent and universal force, as if contemplating a nirvana of absolute and eternal sorrow. Chris Isaak (1987) was an equally compelling show of desolate private masses and unfocused photographs of a distant grey landscape. His art peaked with the…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":246,"text":"…and Leonard Cohen, not Bob Dylan or Bruce Springsteen. One of the most influential styles of the 1990s was the moody and depressed one pioneered by Chris Isaak, Smog and American Music Club in San Francisco. It spread like a disease and almost became a stand-alone genre. Bleak dirges were strummed…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":271,"text":"…keyboards and violin, on Tindersticks (1993). Its songs were the ideal soundtrack for brothels packed with philosophers. Stuart Staples' voice (a Chris Isaak soundalike) was lost in the labyrinth of his own visions, haunted by the giant shadows of Tom Waits, Nick Cave and Leonard Cohen. But the subtlety…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":278,"text":"…monolith 3am Sunday @ Fortune Otto's (1996) that evolved into the solemn and depressed ballads of Mojave (1999), which often sounded like Chris Isaak interpreting Neil Young's Harvest or Bob Dylan's Knocking On Heaven's Door. The alt-country movement spawned singer-songwriters such as Chicago's…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":104144116070442,"type":"album","name":"Silvertone","list_id":103254340346721,"list":"RYM Top — Regional Music — Americana","src":"musthear","rank":74,"year":1985,"note":null,"yt":"kizOgw_sfTg","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":104144116070442,"type":"album","name":"Silvertone","list_id":52032266791182,"list":"Scaruffi 1980s","src":"musthear","rank":315,"year":1985,"note":null,"yt":"kizOgw_sfTg","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":1047818112874,"type":"album","name":"Chris Isaak","list_id":52032266791182,"list":"Scaruffi 1980s","src":"musthear","rank":314,"year":1987,"note":null,"yt":"PwGR9AQfRB4","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":137898908612537,"type":"song","name":"Wicked Game","work_year":1991,"l